   "id": "el-0103",
   "seed": 11192351,
   "versionNonce": 232916071,
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1554,
   "y": 2827.45,
   "width": 1352,
   "height": 20.74,
   "strokeColor": "#1a1d23",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "text": "Why it is worth building, and how it stays free",
   "originalText": "Why it is worth building, and how it stays free",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.22,
   "autoResize": false,
   "baseline": 13.600000000000001
  },
  {
   "isDeleted": false,
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "version": 1,
   "id": "el-0104",
   "seed": 1715012418,
   "versionNonce": 1787452380,
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1554,
   "y": 2856.1899999999996,
   "width": 1352,
   "height": 289.68,
   "strokeColor": "#495057",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "text": "True is the ONLY one of the five with real faceted search\n(/advanced-search). At 300+ model codes this stops being a\nnice-to-have: a flat list is unusable, and a category grid alone\ncannot answer \"two-door undercounter freezer under 900 mm wide\".\n\nFREE-TIER IMPLEMENTATION\n  Facets are COLUMNS plus a GIN index, not a search service.\n  tsvector + pg_trgm behind the text box.\n  Filter state lives in the URL, so a filtered view is linkable,\n  crawlable and CDN-cacheable.\n  ISR-render only the ~40 most common facet combinations; the\n  long tail resolves client-side against a ~60 KB static index.\n  A visitor filtering the catalogue never wakes Postgres.\n\nSWAP POINT   lib/search.ts -> Typesense when facet COUNTS and\n  typo tolerance are wanted. Same search(q, facets) signature,\n  so no call site changes.  (Seam 10, \u00a78.)",
   "originalText": "True is the ONLY one of the five with real faceted search\n(/advanced-search). At 300+ model codes this stops being a\nnice-to-have: a flat list is unusable, and a category grid alone\ncannot answer \"two-door undercounter freezer under 900 mm wide\".\n\nFREE-TIER IMPLEMENTATION\n  Facets are COLUMNS plus a GIN index, not a search service.\n  tsvector + pg_trgm behind the text box.\n  Filter state lives in the URL, so a filtered view is linkable,\n  crawlable and CDN-cacheable.\n  ISR-render only the ~40 most common facet combinations; the\n  long tail resolves client-side against a ~60 KB static index.\n  A visitor filtering the catalogue never wakes Postgres.\n\nSWAP POINT   lib/search.ts -> Typesense when facet COUNTS and\n  typo tolerance are wanted. Same search(q, facets) signature,\n  so no call site changes.  (Seam 10, \u00a78.)",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.42,
   "autoResize": false,
   "baseline": 9.600000000000001
  },
  {
   "isDeleted": false,
