   "id": "el-0331",
   "seed": 1511911200,
   "versionNonce": 124358739,
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1484,
   "y": 6392.27,
   "width": 1422,
   "height": 528.24,
   "strokeColor": "#495057",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "text": "LEAVE OUT                      FOUND ON       WHY NOT\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSerial number lookup           True           needs an installed base\n4 separate warranty forms      True           one service form covers it\nParts e-commerce + tracking    True, Bev-Air  a whole storefront\nAccount login / cart           Bev-Air        no prices means no cart\n\"Build & price\" configurator    none           0 of 5 publish a price\nInvestor relations             Blue Star      not your obligation\nGovernance / group companies   Blue Star      conglomerate noise\nSeparate Sustainability page   3 of 5         a section inside About\nSeparate R&D / Factories       2 of 5         sections inside About\nSeparate press-release feed    2 of 5         one News feed\nWhite paper library            Traulsen       needs real research\nVideo library page             Bev-Air, Trau. embed on the product page\n6 separate industry pages      True (14!)     one page, six anchors\nMulti-slide hero carousel      2 of 5         slides 2+ are not seen\nHorizontal-scroll showcase     index.html \u00a76  no sales function\n\nTHE RULE: every page ships with content on day one. Nine complete pages\nbeat twenty-five pages where eighteen say \"coming soon\" -- which is how\ncopying True's support tree would leave you.\n\nALSO CUT FROM THE CURRENT index.html (report \u00a711):\n  \u00a75  \"build & price\" CTA        implies pricing -> [Request a Quote]\n  \u00a76  horizontal-scroll section  420vh of scroll-jacking, no sales job\n  \u00a77  \"Try it for free!\" CTA     a SaaS pattern inherited from unox.com.\n                                 You cannot try a refrigerator for free.\n  \u00a79  merge into \u00a74              \"choose by type\" duplicates the rail\n  ADD a client logo strip        missing, and the cheapest credibility\n                                 available on the page.\n  Net: thirteen sections -> ten. The page gets shorter and converts better.",
   "originalText": "LEAVE OUT                      FOUND ON       WHY NOT\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSerial number lookup           True           needs an installed base\n4 separate warranty forms      True           one service form covers it\nParts e-commerce + tracking    True, Bev-Air  a whole storefront\nAccount login / cart           Bev-Air        no prices means no cart\n\"Build & price\" configurator    none           0 of 5 publish a price\nInvestor relations             Blue Star      not your obligation\nGovernance / group companies   Blue Star      conglomerate noise\nSeparate Sustainability page   3 of 5         a section inside About\nSeparate R&D / Factories       2 of 5         sections inside About\nSeparate press-release feed    2 of 5         one News feed\nWhite paper library            Traulsen       needs real research\nVideo library page             Bev-Air, Trau. embed on the product page\n6 separate industry pages      True (14!)     one page, six anchors\nMulti-slide hero carousel      2 of 5         slides 2+ are not seen\nHorizontal-scroll showcase     index.html \u00a76  no sales function\n\nTHE RULE: every page ships with content on day one. Nine complete pages\nbeat twenty-five pages where eighteen say \"coming soon\" -- which is how\ncopying True's support tree would leave you.\n\nALSO CUT FROM THE CURRENT index.html (report \u00a711):\n  \u00a75  \"build & price\" CTA        implies pricing -> [Request a Quote]\n  \u00a76  horizontal-scroll section  420vh of scroll-jacking, no sales job\n  \u00a77  \"Try it for free!\" CTA     a SaaS pattern inherited from unox.com.\n                                 You cannot try a refrigerator for free.\n  \u00a79  merge into \u00a74              \"choose by type\" duplicates the rail\n  ADD a client logo strip        missing, and the cheapest credibility\n                                 available on the page.\n  Net: thirteen sections -> ten. The page gets shorter and converts better.",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.42,
   "autoResize": false,
   "baseline": 9.600000000000001
  },
